Why no extra Vite plugins were needed for this project:
- CSS is handled natively by Vite — no css-loader/style-loader/mini-css-extract needed.
- Modern JS transpilation is built in via esbuild — no Babel required.
- .env files are supported out of the box via import.meta.env — no dotenv-webpack.
- HTML entry point is auto-discovered if index.html exists at the project root.

One thing to note: Vite uses index.html as the entry point directly (not a JS entry passed via config). If your current webpack.config.js points to a JS entry file, you may need to add a minimal vite.config.js or ensure index.html exists and references your JS via a <script type="module"> tag. Let me know if you want help with that migration step.

